```
lim_{x	o a} rac{\sqrt{x+a}-\sqrt{a}}{x-a}
```
Multiplying by the conjugate gives

```
= lim_{x	o a} rac{(x+a)-a}{(x-a)(\sqrt{x+a}+\sqrt{a})}
= lim_{x	o a} rac{x}{(x-a)(\sqrt{x+a}+\sqrt{a})}
```
After cancelling the factor \((x-a)\) the limit evaluates to \( rac{3}{4}

**Odds in Favour and Odds in Against**

If in a random experiment, total number of outcomes is $n$ out of which $m$ are favourable to an event $A$, then

odds in favour of $A =  rac{m}{n-m}$

and odds against of $A =  rac{n-m}{m}$

$	herefore P(A) =  rac{	ext{Number of favourable cases to } A}{	ext{Total number of cases}} =  rac{m}{n}$

and $P( ar{A}) = 1 - P(A) = 1 -  rac{m}{n} =  rac{n-m}{n}$

### Key Formulas
- odds \text{ in favour of } A = \frac{m}{n-m}
- odds \text{ against of } A = \frac{n-m}{m}
- P(A) = \frac{\text{Number of favourable cases to } A}{\text{Total number of cases}} = \frac{m}{n}
- P(\bar{A}) = 1 - P(A) = 1 - \frac{m}{n} = \frac{n-m}{n}
